(b) (i) open and maintain an Index Register for each
of the following types of Warrant Books;
Time Allowed Commitment Warrant Book
Affiliation/Maintenance Warrant Book and 
First Instance Warrant Index Book;
(ii) the Index Register shall be drawn up in
accordance with the specimen shown at
“Appendix K” and shall reflect the person’s
name, surname, alias(es), serial number of the
warrant and warrant number;
(c) ensure that on the receipt of every warrant, a
record of the particulars is made in the relevant
Index and Warrant Book;
(d) record in the General Warrant Book all informa-
tion relating to warrants other than—
(i) Time Allowed Commitment Warrant;
(ii) Affiliation/Maintenance Warrant;
(iii) Ejectment Warrant;
(e) record all the particulars of a Bench Warrant in the
General Warrant Book in red ink;
(f) whenever a warrant is executed or transferred to
another Station, draw a red line through the entry
in the relevant Warrant Book;
(g) Submit to the Second Division Officer in Charge
of each Division/Branch/Section daily Warrant
execution/transfer/returned Information;
(h) at the end of the year, draw a diagonal red line
beneath the last entry in each Warrant Register
indicating along the said line the end of that
particular year;
TRINIDAD  AND  TOBAGO  POLICE  SERVICE 23
